1
00:00:01,033 --> 00:00:04,967
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,467
<i>Previously on You're
My Favorite Song.</i>

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:14,767
<i>Sell this resort to me, or we're
going to have a problem.</i>

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:19,333
<i>For almost 17 years, Serina,
you never reached out to us.</i>

5
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:21,367
<i> We've been looking for you.</i>

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,567
<i>Why would you even look
for me,</i>

7
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,133
<i>when you already have your
favorite child with you?</i>

8
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:27,500
<i> Come on, my child.</i>

9
00:00:27,633 --> 00:00:28,967
<i> Stop calling me "child."</i>

10
00:00:30,067 --> 00:00:33,933
<i>Is the story
about the missing princess</i>

11
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:37,167
<i> of the Montaverde family true?</i>

12
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:41,467
<i>The Montaverde princess
is truly missing.</i>

13
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,500
<i>I can feel it,
that she's still alive.</i>

14
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:47,133
<i>And I'm sure
that Celestine inherited</i>

15
00:00:47,267 --> 00:00:51,067
<i>her father's courage
and her mother's intelligence.</i>

16
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,133
<i>On Celestine's first birthday...</i>

17
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:57,867
[VASE CLATTERS]

18
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
<i>She was kidnapped
by unknown men.</i>

19
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:03,000
<i>When Ma'am Isabella
passed away...</i>

20
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:04,000
<i> Isabella...</i>

21
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:07,600
<i>the mansion lost all its color.</i>

22
00:01:07,767 --> 00:01:11,900
<i> For the first time in the
history of Brighton Bay Academy,</i>

23
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:15,600
<i>someone has answered
my bonus question.</i>

24
00:01:15,733 --> 00:01:16,833
<i> [INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

25
00:01:16,967 --> 00:01:19,267
<i> Miss Angel Dimaculangan?</i>

26
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,667
<i>- [STUDENTS MURMURING]
- What?</i>

27
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,033
<i>One hundred fifty
out of one hundred.</i>

28
00:01:26,633 --> 00:01:28,467
<i> And I think</i>

29
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:35,200
<i>we now have a new top student
here at Brighton Bay Academy.</i>

30
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:37,933
<i>You're supposed to distribute
our test papers, right?</i>

31
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:38,967
<i> So pick them up.</i>

32
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:40,567
<i> Let me help you, Angel.</i>

33
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,267
<i>Hopefully you won't drop
it again next time.</i>

34
00:01:49,433 --> 00:01:52,033
<i>Your new house in Solmera
City is beautiful.</i>

35
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:54,367
<i>I'll continue busking
here in Solmera.</i>

36
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:56,667
<i>Maybe I'll do it in front
of Brighton Bay Academy.</i>

37
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,400
<i> Who's that girl again?</i>

38
00:01:58,533 --> 00:01:59,600
<i> Angel?</i>

39
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:03,133
<i>I wonder if I'll see her again.</i>

40
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:05,133
<i> I just want to busk here.</i>

41
00:02:05,267 --> 00:02:07,233
<i> I'm just hoping, Jacob.</i>

42
00:02:07,367 --> 00:02:09,067
<i>That Angel might be
at Manila Park</i>

43
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,067
<i>since that's where
you met before?</i>

44
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,900
<i> Miguel,</i>

45
00:02:15,033 --> 00:02:16,800
<i> what are you doing here</i>

46
00:02:16,933 --> 00:02:19,267
<i> wearing that stupid costume?</i>

47
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:23,667
[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

48
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:31,067
<i>♪'Cause baby,
you are my favorite song ♪</i>

49
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:34,367
<i>♪ I'll put you on repeat
all night ♪</i>

50
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:38,400
<i> ♪ I know I'll never move on ♪</i>

51
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:42,067
<i>♪ My first,
right where I belong ♪</i>

52
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:48,833
<i>♪ You are my first
heartbeat song ♪</i>

53
00:02:53,967 --> 00:02:56,133
What if someone recognizes you?

54
00:02:56,267 --> 00:02:57,833
Dad, I've been doing this
for months, okay?

55
00:02:57,967 --> 00:02:59,100
And I'm fine.

56
00:02:59,233 --> 00:03:01,433
No one's catching me anyway.

57
00:03:01,567 --> 00:03:04,733
I just want to sing
without anyone recognizing me.

58
00:03:04,867 --> 00:03:06,667
That's who I was before
I became famous, right?

59
00:03:07,967 --> 00:03:09,667
- [CLICKS TONGUE]
- You will not

60
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,367
waste your time like this.

61
00:03:12,933 --> 00:03:14,133
Today is my rest day.

62
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,500
Rest day?

63
00:03:18,267 --> 00:03:20,267
It's your rest day
and you're out singing.

64
00:03:21,267 --> 00:03:22,333
You've got a lot of energy,

65
00:03:22,467 --> 00:03:24,300
so why don't you go back
to the studio,

66
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:28,467
meet up with your bandmates
and finish your album?

67
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,500
Right?

68
00:03:30,933 --> 00:03:32,667
Jacob, you too.

69
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,933
Sorry, Sir Neil.

70
00:03:34,067 --> 00:03:35,267
Fix this.

71
00:03:39,733 --> 00:03:41,067
I told you.

72
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:45,667
[POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:56,933
You should've listened to me.

74
00:04:05,033 --> 00:04:05,867
[JACOB CLICKS TONGUE]

75
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,133
Can you just behave

76
00:04:10,267 --> 00:04:11,567
for once?

77
00:04:12,767 --> 00:04:14,200
Now your dad's mad.

78
00:04:24,033 --> 00:04:25,200
Charm,

79
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:27,467
your test paper.

80
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,033
Congrats,

81
00:04:30,167 --> 00:04:31,767
85 out of 100.

82
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,433
We got the same score.

83
00:04:33,567 --> 00:04:37,900
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:04:38,033 --> 00:04:39,233
Thank you.

85
00:04:40,933 --> 00:04:41,900
Loser.

86
00:04:42,033 --> 00:04:45,500
- [SOFT TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ADIE CHUCKLES]

87
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:34,367
Sir Enrico,

88
00:05:34,533 --> 00:05:36,733
- you've been working all week,
- Lady Mara.

89
00:05:36,867 --> 00:05:38,900
The doctor said you need
to rest.

90
00:05:39,867 --> 00:05:42,600
- [SIGHS]
- You know me, Lady Mara.

91
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:45,567
Ever since Celestine and...

92
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:47,567
Isabella,

93
00:05:49,233 --> 00:05:51,700
I've devoted all my time to...

94
00:05:51,833 --> 00:05:52,967
the business.

95
00:05:56,067 --> 00:05:57,333
Please don't worry, Sir.

96
00:05:57,467 --> 00:06:01,300
We never stop praying
that Celestine is still alive.

97
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:07,367
And that one day,
our princess will return.

98
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,333
Thank you.

99
00:06:11,467 --> 00:06:13,467
Sir, would you like some coffee?

100
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,433
- [EXHALES]
- No, Lady Mara.

101
00:06:15,567 --> 00:06:17,733
Could I just have
brandy instead?

102
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:18,700
Ah, yes, Sir.

103
00:06:19,667 --> 00:06:22,800
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

104
00:06:22,933 --> 00:06:23,867
[BOTTLE CORK POPS]

105
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,367
Sir.

106
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,833
Kindly return this.

107
00:06:32,967 --> 00:06:33,833
Thank you.

108
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,567
Unfortunately, my family
still refuses to sell.

109
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:42,300
And their cheap hotel
is opening in two days.

110
00:06:42,467 --> 00:06:45,000
And your property has the best
sunset view

111
00:06:45,133 --> 00:06:47,167
in all of Solmera City.

112
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:48,367
If we acquire it,

113
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:52,100
our investor in Dubai will
definitely be pleased.

114
00:06:52,233 --> 00:06:53,933
- [CLICKS TONGUE]
- I know.

115
00:06:54,067 --> 00:06:57,033
Don't worry, I'll continue
the negotiations.

116
00:07:00,033 --> 00:07:02,200
You're drinking again?

117
00:07:02,333 --> 00:07:03,333
[SIGHS]

118
00:07:03,467 --> 00:07:05,300
Let me guess.

119
00:07:05,433 --> 00:07:08,067
You're thinking about
your child again.

120
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,900
There you go again, Enrico.

121
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:16,467
Today, marks 16 years since...

122
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,400
Celestine disappeared.

123
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:23,133
It's not wrong to

124
00:07:23,267 --> 00:07:25,800
keep hoping that even now

125
00:07:25,933 --> 00:07:27,433
she's still alive

126
00:07:27,567 --> 00:07:29,200
and I'll find my child.

127
00:07:29,333 --> 00:07:31,900
- [SCOFFS]
- Oh, my God.

128
00:07:32,033 --> 00:07:35,800
Are you seriously saying that
to my face?

129
00:07:35,933 --> 00:07:37,533
I'm your wife now

130
00:07:37,667 --> 00:07:40,100
and Celestine is presumed dead.

131
00:07:40,233 --> 00:07:42,267
You're just wasting your time.

132
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,333
You can't even give me a child.

133
00:07:44,467 --> 00:07:46,333
Maybe subconsciously,

134
00:07:46,467 --> 00:07:47,900
you don't want to replace her
in your heart

135
00:07:48,067 --> 00:07:51,600
that's why no matter how we try
to have a baby, we can't!

136
00:07:51,733 --> 00:07:52,867
- My God.
- No, no.

137
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,467
Serina, Serina.

138
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:59,500
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:08:20,367 --> 00:08:25,967
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

140
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,733
I don't like her.

141
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:33,633
She acts like
she's someone important,

142
00:08:33,767 --> 00:08:35,967
when she just got lucky
on the exam.

143
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,467
I know.

144
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:42,000
What newcomer scores higher than
a perfect score?

145
00:08:42,133 --> 00:08:43,500
It's so unbelievable.

146
00:08:43,633 --> 00:08:45,700
I mean, I wonder what her cheat
code is.

147
00:08:45,833 --> 00:08:46,733
I know.

148
00:08:51,133 --> 00:08:53,000
Just ignore them.

149
00:08:54,833 --> 00:08:56,833
- Siklab!
- [GIGGLES]

150
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:00,300
This is our row for today.

151
00:09:00,433 --> 00:09:01,700
Did you hear that?

152
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:04,967
- You heard that, right? Move.
- Oh my! That was intense, girl.

153
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,400
[GIGGLES]

154
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:10,133
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

155
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:14,333
Do you see?

156
00:09:14,467 --> 00:09:16,567
Do you see his eyes clearly?

157
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,733
Why do you always keep
looking at Charm?

158
00:09:18,867 --> 00:09:20,267
Do you have a crush on her?

159
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,533
- Yeah.
- [CHUCKLES]

160
00:09:22,667 --> 00:09:24,600
No, but...

161
00:09:24,733 --> 00:09:26,933
That's not important.

162
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:30,167
What matters is you should know
that aside from Calix,

163
00:09:31,867 --> 00:09:35,067
she's someone you shouldn't
mess with.

164
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,200
[SOFT TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

165
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:37,867
What do you mean?

166
00:09:45,633 --> 00:09:47,600
I like them both,
if Calix is super smart...

167
00:09:48,867 --> 00:09:51,533
- Aside from Calix,
- [SOFT TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:09:51,667 --> 00:09:53,933
she's someone you shouldn't
go up against.

169
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:57,633
What do you mean?

170
00:10:03,867 --> 00:10:07,400
In our section, there's
a hierarchy everyone follows.

171
00:10:07,533 --> 00:10:09,533
Like I told you earlier,

172
00:10:09,667 --> 00:10:12,800
the seating arrangements here
have meaning.

173
00:10:12,933 --> 00:10:15,067
And that's something you need
to understand, Angel.

174
00:10:18,033 --> 00:10:20,467
If you're seated in row one,

175
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:23,800
from there to the end,

176
00:10:23,933 --> 00:10:28,067
you're usually considered
one of the "losers."

177
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:33,567
Like me, a bit shy,
kind of awkward.

178
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,467
[CHUCKLES]

179
00:10:35,633 --> 00:10:39,233
Also those who easily
get panic attacks.

180
00:10:40,967 --> 00:10:43,933
Those with poor eyesight
and frequent illnesses.

181
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:49,267
In short,

182
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:52,533
the ones in row one are those
who need special attention

183
00:10:52,667 --> 00:10:55,400
so they can be rushed
to the clinic quickly.

184
00:10:55,533 --> 00:10:57,600
What about me in row two?

185
00:10:57,733 --> 00:11:00,733
That's where Miss Dragona
placed me yesterday.

186
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:08,200
Your row
is for the smartest students.

187
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,900
That's why you're seated
near Calix.

188
00:11:24,033 --> 00:11:28,367
He's brought many awards
to Brighton Academy.

189
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:31,167
He's the best student on campus.

190
00:11:32,467 --> 00:11:33,767
But...

191
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:39,200
it looks like that might be
you now.

192
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:40,633
Even so.

193
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:44,200
Calix is still capable of a lot.

194
00:11:45,467 --> 00:11:46,667
Like what?

195
00:11:47,667 --> 00:11:49,433
Like getting everything
he wants.

196
00:11:56,833 --> 00:11:58,467
As for row three,

197
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,867
those are the average students.

198
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,433
The ones who are just okay,

199
00:12:02,567 --> 00:12:04,333
easygoing in life,

200
00:12:04,467 --> 00:12:06,000
those who just
don't want stress.

201
00:12:06,133 --> 00:12:09,000
A lot of them come from
wealthy families.

202
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:11,733
But they're tight as a group.

203
00:12:11,867 --> 00:12:13,767
If you mess with one of them,

204
00:12:14,833 --> 00:12:16,067
they'll all come
after you together.

205
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,200
[ADIE AND CHARM SQUEALS]

206
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:22,533
- Oh my gosh, he's so handsome!
- I want to see Miguel in person

207
00:12:22,667 --> 00:12:24,100
at their concert here
in Solmera City.

208
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:25,200
What?

209
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:26,533
- He's so handsome, Adie.
- Oh my God, oh, wait.

210
00:12:26,667 --> 00:12:27,933
Oh my gosh.

211
00:12:28,067 --> 00:12:30,700
I thought Calix was your type?

212
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:35,433
Well,

213
00:12:35,567 --> 00:12:36,967
I like them both.

214
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:41,167
If Calix is super smart,
then Miguel is super talented.

215
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:43,933
Imagine, he's not just
the main vocalist,

216
00:12:44,067 --> 00:12:46,300
he's also the writer of all
Siklab's hit songs.

217
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:47,200
[CHUCKLES]

218
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:49,567
- Oh my God.
- That's why I like him.

219
00:12:49,733 --> 00:12:51,833
- I like them.
- Oh my gosh, he's so cute.

220
00:12:51,967 --> 00:12:53,033
- Yeah.
- Look at that.

221
00:12:53,167 --> 00:12:54,833
- [CHARM SQUEALS]
- [ADIE GASPS]

222
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,533
<i> And his looks, Siklab.</i>

223
00:12:58,667 --> 00:13:00,367
[ADIE AND CHARM SQUEALING]

224
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:03,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,867
Those are Calix's group
in row four.

226
00:13:07,967 --> 00:13:10,800
Row four is the most
hated section.

227
00:13:11,567 --> 00:13:13,133
Because

228
00:13:13,267 --> 00:13:15,100
that's where teachers put
the troublemakers

229
00:13:15,233 --> 00:13:17,367
and the ones
with the lowest grades.

230
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:18,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:13:18,967 --> 00:13:20,667
That's why they all

232
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,933
follow Calix.

233
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:25,767
Because if Calix didn't
let them copy,

234
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,233
they'd probably

235
00:13:28,367 --> 00:13:30,833
have been expelled from Brighton
Academy a long time ago.

236
00:13:30,967 --> 00:13:36,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

237
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:52,900
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

238
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,767
[EXHALES]

239
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:57,333
[TYRONE EXHALES]

240
00:14:04,833 --> 00:14:06,333
Do you love me, Serina?

241
00:14:08,267 --> 00:14:10,600
What kind of question is that?

242
00:14:10,733 --> 00:14:12,067
Of course.

243
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:14,300
But I'm married, Tyrone.

244
00:14:19,367 --> 00:14:21,367
The only thing Enrico
has over me

245
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:22,767
is that he's a billionaire.

246
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:23,800
[SCOFFS]

247
00:14:23,933 --> 00:14:26,067
Stop being insecure about that.

248
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:29,167
You know I was miserable
with him.

249
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:33,933
He's either busy with work or
grieving for his missing child

250
00:14:34,067 --> 00:14:36,067
who was kidnapped
by a syndicate.

251
00:14:36,767 --> 00:14:41,000
But everything changed
when I met you two years ago.

252
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:44,767
Honestly, I wish you were
the one in Enrico's place.

253
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:47,467
Then why don't
we just switch places?

254
00:14:48,867 --> 00:14:50,367
Huh? What do you mean?

255
00:14:53,233 --> 00:14:55,533
Isn't Enrico all alone in life?

256
00:14:55,667 --> 00:14:59,200
And his family is already
torn apart because of business.

257
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:02,133
So technically,
if something happens to him,

258
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:03,900
all his wealth will go to you.

259
00:15:04,033 --> 00:15:06,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:15:06,733 --> 00:15:09,833
Are you suggesting
we kill Enrico?

261
00:15:09,967 --> 00:15:13,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

262
00:15:13,867 --> 00:15:16,500
I have a lot
of connections, Serina.

263
00:15:16,633 --> 00:15:18,100
It doesn't matter if

264
00:15:18,233 --> 00:15:20,100
Enrico is an army reservist.

265
00:15:21,067 --> 00:15:23,233
I know someone who works clean.

266
00:15:26,733 --> 00:15:27,900
- [CLICKS TONGUE]
- You know what,

267
00:15:28,033 --> 00:15:30,100
let's just go home.

268
00:15:30,233 --> 00:15:33,067
Let's go back to the mansion
before Enrico suspects anything.

269
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:35,233
And make sure to clean up, okay?

270
00:15:36,833 --> 00:15:38,033
[EXHALES]

271
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:42,033
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

272
00:16:16,367 --> 00:16:17,267
Dad,

273
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,433
our grand opening
is still a day away,

274
00:16:19,567 --> 00:16:22,333
so why do you already
look defeated?

275
00:16:24,467 --> 00:16:25,467
No, my child.

276
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,300
I was just thinking
about Serina.

277
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:34,367
Her anger toward us
is so intense.

278
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:35,900
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

279
00:16:36,033 --> 00:16:37,933
What can we do?

280
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:43,133
Do you want me to talk
to her, Dad?

281
00:16:44,967 --> 00:16:48,233
I'll tell her about your cancer.

282
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,300
So she'll finally come
to her senses.

283
00:16:53,033 --> 00:16:55,300
I don't want it that way.

284
00:16:55,433 --> 00:16:56,767
Beverly,

285
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:58,167
I don't want

286
00:16:58,300 --> 00:16:59,867
her to come back to the family

287
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,300
just because she feels
forced to because

288
00:17:02,433 --> 00:17:06,100
I'm sick or because she thinks
I'm dying.

289
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:07,733
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

290
00:17:07,867 --> 00:17:09,567
I still have a long life
ahead of me.

291
00:17:11,033 --> 00:17:13,733
And if she comes back out
of obligation,

292
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:15,200
you know

293
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:17,400
what will happen when I'm gone?

294
00:17:17,533 --> 00:17:19,333
You'll just end up
fighting again.

295
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:23,133
I want our family
to truly reconcile,

296
00:17:23,267 --> 00:17:26,900
a genuine reconciliation,

297
00:17:27,033 --> 00:17:28,700
where we truly understand
each other.

298
00:17:28,833 --> 00:17:30,533
Not just the two of us,

299
00:17:32,567 --> 00:17:34,200
but you two as well.

300
00:17:37,533 --> 00:17:38,267
All right?

301
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:42,533
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

302
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:07,300
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

303
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:20,400
Here's the payment.

304
00:18:21,933 --> 00:18:24,867
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,467
I'll add more,

306
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,833
just make sure
you do your job well.

307
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:36,800
Here's the payment.

308
00:18:36,933 --> 00:18:40,200
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

309
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:45,600
I'll add more, just make sure
you do your job well.

310
00:18:46,767 --> 00:18:48,467
Leave it to us, Miss Serina.

311
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:50,467
Their grand opening
will not happen.

312
00:18:51,767 --> 00:18:53,467
Just make sure of it.

313
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:54,833
Make sure

314
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,600
you ruin Gran Vista Resort.

315
00:18:57,733 --> 00:18:58,633
Yes, Ma'am.

316
00:18:59,867 --> 00:19:01,200
All right, leave now.

317
00:19:01,333 --> 00:19:05,567
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:06,900
[SERINA EXHALES]

319
00:19:07,033 --> 00:19:08,767
The kids I hired are good.

320
00:19:10,367 --> 00:19:12,667
Even if they get caught,

321
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:14,167
they won't be jailed

322
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:15,633
since they're minors.

323
00:19:17,767 --> 00:19:19,367
Thank you, Tyrone.

324
00:19:24,033 --> 00:19:25,700
I'll do anything for you,

325
00:19:25,833 --> 00:19:26,867
Serina.

326
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:49,267
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

327
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:01,133
Good thing Ma'am Perez
is absent,

328
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:03,167
we get to hang out here
on the roof deck.

329
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,700
Hey!

330
00:20:06,833 --> 00:20:08,000
You like me, right?

331
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:09,433
Can you get my water?

332
00:20:09,567 --> 00:20:11,000
Of course.

333
00:20:11,133 --> 00:20:15,300
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

334
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:37,733
Oh no,

335
00:20:37,867 --> 00:20:39,533
where are our bags?

336
00:20:39,667 --> 00:20:41,733
My mom will be so mad
if I lose it.

337
00:20:41,867 --> 00:20:44,500
- [SIGHS]
- That bag is important to me.

338
00:20:44,633 --> 00:20:45,667
Where is it?

339
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:00,467
Yours is the blue one, right?

340
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,567
Yeah, Yours is the brown one,
right?

341
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:03,800
Yes.

342
00:21:06,233 --> 00:21:07,967
Hey! Is that it?

343
00:21:11,367 --> 00:21:13,333
- Oh no!
- Why is it here?

344
00:21:13,467 --> 00:21:15,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:21:15,267 --> 00:21:16,400
Who threw this?

346
00:21:16,533 --> 00:21:19,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

347
00:21:19,867 --> 00:21:20,900
Calix.

348
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:25,933
Why?

349
00:21:26,067 --> 00:21:27,333
Do you have a problem?

350
00:21:27,467 --> 00:21:28,800
Did you throw this?

351
00:21:28,933 --> 00:21:32,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:21:34,867 --> 00:21:36,667
Yes.

353
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:38,167
Got a complaint?

354
00:21:38,300 --> 00:21:39,533
What is your problem?

355
00:21:39,667 --> 00:21:40,967
What did I ever do to you?

356
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:42,733
I just wanted to check your bag.

357
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,833
Maybe you had cheat notes.

358
00:21:45,967 --> 00:21:47,733
I mean, are you really smart?

359
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:49,800
Or are you just getting lucky?

360
00:21:50,933 --> 00:21:51,867
Or maybe...

361
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:54,667
Maybe I'm right.

362
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,633
- That you're cheating!
- I'm not a cheater.

363
00:21:57,767 --> 00:21:58,800
Let's see then.

364
00:22:00,133 --> 00:22:01,600
In the absence
of air resistance,

365
00:22:01,733 --> 00:22:03,633
which force causes all objects
in free fall

366
00:22:03,767 --> 00:22:05,767
to accelerate at the same rate
regardless of mass?

367
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:06,667
Gravity.

368
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:08,433
If a species
has no natural predators

369
00:22:08,567 --> 00:22:10,267
and unlimited resources,

370
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,800
what growth pattern
will it show initially?

371
00:22:11,933 --> 00:22:14,633
It will exhibit
exponential growth.

372
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,767
My turn.

373
00:22:18,133 --> 00:22:19,800
If an object
has constant velocity,

374
00:22:19,933 --> 00:22:22,667
what can be said about the net
force acting on it?

375
00:22:25,867 --> 00:22:27,433
The net force is zero.

376
00:22:29,933 --> 00:22:31,533
I know that.

377
00:22:31,667 --> 00:22:33,433
I was just about to answer.

378
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:36,633
That just means you're slow.

379
00:22:36,767 --> 00:22:39,567
You're not as good
as you think you are, Calix.

380
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,400
Out of all the people

381
00:22:43,533 --> 00:22:45,933
you could go up against here
at Brighton Bay Academy,

382
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,100
you chose me?

383
00:22:48,233 --> 00:22:50,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

384
00:22:50,567 --> 00:22:52,567
I'm not afraid of you, Calix.

385
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:56,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

386
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Wrong answer.

387
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:11,600
Because you should be.

388
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:26,167
Do it, Calix.

389
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:27,267
Punch her.

390
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:28,967
Yeah, she deserves it.

391
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:30,467
Go, go.

392
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:33,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

393
00:23:34,933 --> 00:23:38,167
Find out tomorrow on You're My
Favorite Song...

394
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:40,033
This is the one I wanted.

395
00:23:40,167 --> 00:23:41,400
There, it's simple.

396
00:23:41,533 --> 00:23:42,767
That one.

397
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:46,200
But that one has already
been sold.

398
00:23:46,333 --> 00:23:48,067
The person who bought it

399
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:50,067
is someone dear to you.

400
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,400
- Really?
- Yes.

401
00:23:51,533 --> 00:23:52,867
Your wife.

402
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,367
Tell me the truth.

403
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:56,967
Are you having an affair
with Tyrone?

404
00:23:57,100 --> 00:23:59,833
[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:23:59,967 --> 00:24:02,000
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

406
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,333
Hey!

407
00:24:05,467 --> 00:24:07,667
- Who are you?
- Hey! What are you doing?

408
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:09,600
[GRIPPING MUSIC CONTINUES]

409
00:24:09,733 --> 00:24:12,200
We'll go through every room
and every door here.

410
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:13,833
- All right.
- Until I find them.

411
00:24:13,967 --> 00:24:14,933
[PHONE CHIMES]

412
00:24:15,067 --> 00:24:16,033
Hey.

413
00:24:16,167 --> 00:24:17,800
[CHIMING CONTINUES]

414
00:24:20,967 --> 00:24:22,300
It's Mom Bebe.

415
00:24:22,433 --> 00:24:24,667
- [LINE RINGING]
- I wonder why she's calling.

416
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:29,200
- Hey! My bag!
- For three!

417
00:24:29,367 --> 00:24:30,933
[BAG THUDS]

418
00:24:31,067 --> 00:24:32,867
Wait, This bag...

419
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,400
I know this bag.

420
00:24:34,533 --> 00:24:35,733
There! Someone took my bag,

421
00:24:35,867 --> 00:24:41,167
- Zion.
- ♪ I'm still searching ♪

422
00:24:41,300 --> 00:24:46,567
♪ In case you come back to... ♪
